✅ MASTER AGENT PROMPT
MimiPro — Employee, Salary, Advance & Product Deduction System (A–Z)

You are building the Employee Payroll & Advance Calculation System for a distributor app called MimiPro.

This system must be accurate, auditable, offline-first, and simple because it will be used daily by a business owner.

1️⃣ CORE IDEA (Balaji-Style Calculation)

Employees may:

Work daily or monthly

Take cash advances

Take products in advance (rice, oil, goods, etc.)

Return money later or get deductions from salary

The system must:

Track everything separately

Then combine all deductions at salary time

Never lose historical data

2️⃣ EMPLOYEE TYPES

Each employee has:

employeeId
name
role (deliveryman | helper | staff)
salaryType (daily | monthly)
salaryRate
loginPassword
active

Salary Types
Daily Salary
salary = presentDays × dailyRate

Monthly Salary
salary = fixedMonthlyRate

3️⃣ ATTENDANCE SYSTEM (Salary Foundation)

Attendance is the base of salary.

Attendance Record
attendanceId
employeeId
date (YYYY-MM-DD)
status (present | absent)
linkedDeliveryId (optional)


Rules:

Only one attendance per employee per day

Delivery auto-marks attendance

Manual override allowed (owner only)

4️⃣ CASH ADVANCE SYSTEM

Employees may take cash before month end.

Advance Record
advanceId
employeeId
amount
date
note
type = "cash"


Rules:

Advance is NOT salary

It is a temporary debt

Deducted at salary calculation time

5️⃣ PRODUCT ADVANCE SYSTEM (VERY IMPORTANT)

Employees may take products instead of cash.

Example:

Rice

Oil

Grocery

Company products

Product Advance Record
productAdvanceId
employeeId
productName
quantity
unitPrice
totalValue
date
type = "product"


Calculation:

totalValue = quantity × unitPrice


This totalValue behaves exactly like a cash advance.

6️⃣ RETURN / REPAYMENT SYSTEM

Employees may:

Repay cash

Return product

Pay partially

Repayment Record
repaymentId
employeeId
amount
date
method (cash | product-return)
note


Rules:

Repayment reduces outstanding balance

Never delete old records

Always append history

7️⃣ TOTAL DEDUCTION LOGIC (CRITICAL)

At salary time:

Step 1: Calculate Gross Salary
grossSalary

Step 2: Calculate Total Advances
totalCashAdvance
+ totalProductAdvance
- totalRepayment
= totalOutstanding

Step 3: Final Payable
payableSalary = grossSalary - totalOutstanding


If:

payableSalary < 0
→ show: “Employee still owes money”

8️⃣ MONTHLY SALARY REPORT (OWNER VIEW)

For each employee show:

Name

Days worked

Gross salary

Cash advances

Product advances

Repayments

Net payable

This report must be:

Filterable by month

Exportable later (optional)

9️⃣ EMPLOYEE LOGIN SYSTEM

Employees can log in to their own account.

Login Model
employeeId
password (hashed)

Employee App Permissions (Read-Only)

Employee can see:

Their attendance

Their salary calculation

Their advances

Their product deductions

Their outstanding balance

Employee CANNOT:

Edit data

See other employees

Delete records

🔐 SECURITY RULES

Each employee ID has a password

Wrong password = no access

Offline login allowed (local auth)

Owner has master access

🔄 DATA FLOW (IMPORTANT)
Delivery
 → Attendance auto-mark
 → Salary base updated

Advance/Product Taken
 → Advance table updated

Repayment
 → Balance reduced

Month End
 → Salary calculation
 → Deduction applied

